## Unit 1

### 제1항 - Greetings
**Lesson objective:** to ask how a person is and understand the answer

#### Vocabulary
- 잡지사 - magazine company
- 방송국 - broadcasting station
- 항공사 - airline company
- 무역회사 - trade company
- 스튜어디스 - flight attendant
- 지내다 - to spend one's time
- 처음 - first
- 즐겁다 - to be happy or enjoyable
- 열심히 - diligently
- 익숙하다 - to be used to
- 건강하다 - to be healthy
- 곧 - soon
- 연휴 - consecutive holidays
- 다녀오다 - to go and then come back
- 오랜만 - after a long time
- 다니다 - to attend
- 걱정 - worry
- 글 - text
- 편지 - letter
- 잊어버리다 - to forget
- 일기 - journal
- 메모 - memo

#### Let's Listen

**1.**
1) 저는 한국에서 바쁘게 지내요.  
   I live a busy life in Korea.

2) 친구들과 재미있게 시간을 보내고 있어요.  
   I am having a good time with my friends.

3) 요즘 한국은 날씨가 많이 더워졌어요. 힘들게 지내요.  
   The weather in Korea has become much warmer. I'm having a hard time.

4) 처음에는 힘들었지만 이제는 한국 음식을 맛있게 먹을 수 있어요.  
   It was difficult at first but now I can enjoy eating Korean food.

**2.**
처음에는 한국 생활이 힘들었지만 이제는 즐겁게 지내요. 한국말을 열심히 공부해서 한국말이 익숙해졌어요. 한국 친구도 많아졌어요. 운동도 많이 해서 건강해졌어요. 하지만 아직 한국 음식에는 익숙해지지 못했어요.

Living in Korea was difficult at first but now I am having a good time. I am used to the Korean language because I studied hard. I've also made a lot of friends. I have also become healthier since I exercise a lot. However, I am still not used to Korean food.

**3-4.**
노라: 타오 씨, 요즘 어떻게 지내세요?  
Nora: Tao, how are you these days?

타오: 저는 즐겁게 지내요. 노라 씨는요?  
Tao: I'm enjoying life. How about you, Nora?

노라: 저는 지난주부터 중국어 공부를 시작했는데 좀 힘들어요.  
Nora: I started studying Chinese from last week and it's a bit hard.

타오: 곧 익숙해질 거예요.  
Tao: You'll soon get used to it.

**5-7.**
주앙: 모두 연휴를 즐겁게 보냈어요? 에릭 씨, 연휴에 뭐 했어요?  
Juang: Have you all enjoyed your holidays? Eric, what did you do during the break?

에릭: 날마다 회사에서 일했어요. 바쁘게 보냈어요. 올리비아 씨는요?  
Eric: I went to work every day. I was busy. How about you, Olivia?

올리비아: 저는 재미없게 지냈어요. 집에서 한국어 공부만 했어요. 주앙 씨는 어떻게 지냈어요?  
Olivia: I didn't have a fun time at all. All I did was study Korean at home. How about you, Juang? How did you spend the time?

주앙: 저는 바다를 보러 부산에 다녀왔어요.  
Juang: I went down to Busan to see the ocean.

에릭: 부산요? 부산은 어땠어요? 저도 부산에 가고 싶었는데….  
Eric: Busan? How was it? I wanted to go to Busan, too.

주앙: 경치가 아름다웠어요, 맛있는 음식도 많았고요. 여행을 하니까 기분도 건강도 좋아졌어요.  
Juang: The scenery was beautiful and there was a lot of good food. My mood and health has improved because of the traveling.

올리비아: 다음에는 우리 셋이 같이 가요.  
Olivia: Next time, let's go together, the three of us.

#### Let's Read

Dear Ms. Suji Choi,

How are you? This is Huang. It has been a long time. How have you been since then? Are you still quite busy with life?

I am having a good time at my hometown. I enjoyed delicious hometown food with my family and also did some traveling with my friends.

The weather in Korea has gotten much colder, hasn't it? I have to return to Korea next month but I'm worried about the weather. I am also worried about speaking Korean. I didn't study while on vacation at my hometown so I forgot a lot.

Nevertheless, I feel happy when I think about going back to Korea. I want to meet you and my friends and enjoy studying Korean again.

2019.12.10

