### 제2항 - Introductions
**Lesson objective:** to understand introductions about jobs and majors.

#### Vocabulary
- 의학 - medical science
- 경제학 - economics
- 국어국문학 - Korean language and literature
- 천문우주학 - astronomy
- 돕다 - to help
- 별 - star
- 고등학교 - senior high school
- 졸업하다 - to graduate
- 신문방송학 - journalism and mass communication
- 전공 - major
- 컴퓨터공학 - computer engineering
- 교수 - professor
- 경영학 - business administration
- 멋있다 - to be fashionable or cool
- 소개 - introduction
- 자기소개서 - personal statement
- 필요하다 - to need
- 및 - and
- 학습 - learning or study
- 아시아 - Asia
- 관심 - interest
- 자세히 - in detail
- 입학하다 - to enter a school
- 이해하다 - to understand
- 생기다 - to come into being
- 유학 - study abroad

#### Let's Listen

**1.**
1) 방송국에 들어가려고 신문방송학을 전공해요.  
   I am majoring in journalism and mass communication so I can enter into a broadcasting station.

2) 컴퓨터공학을 공부하려고 한국에 왔습니다.  
   I came to Korea to study computer engineering.

3) 저는 대학교에 가려고 한국말을 배워요.  
   I am learning Korean so I can go to college.

4) 한국어 교수가 되려고 국어국문학을 공부합니다.  
   I am majoring in Korean language and literature to become a Korean language professor.

**2.**
저는 5년 전에 한국 드라마를 보고 한국어 공부를 시작했어요. 한국어를 공부한 지 4년쯤 됐어요. 그리고 작년에 고등학교를 졸업하고 한국에 왔어요. 한국에 온 지는 네 달 됐어요.

I started studying Korean after watching a Korean drama five years ago. It has been about four years since I've been studying Korean. I came to Korea after I graduated from high school last year. It's been four months since I came to Korea.

**3-4.**
하늘: 존 씨는 왜 경영학을 공부해요?  
Haneul: John, why are you studying business administration?

존: 저는 무역회사를 경영하려고 경영학을 공부해요. 하늘 씨는요?  
John: I am studying business administration so I can manage a trading company. What about you, Haneul?

하늘: 저는 잡지사 기자가 되려고 국어국문학을 공부해요.  
Hanuel: I am studying Korean language and literature so I can become a magazine reporter.

존: 멋있군요. 하늘 씨는 좋은 기자가 될 거예요.  
John: That's so cool. You'll be a great reporter.

**5-7.**
소개하는 사람: 두 사람이 친구가 되면 좋을 것 같아서 소개하는 거예요. 알렉스 씨, 먼저 소개 좀 해 주시겠어요?  
Introducer: I am introducing you to each other because I thought you could be friends. Alex, can you introduce yourself first?

남자: 안녕하세요? 저는 미국에서 온 알렉스입니다. 미국에서는 방송국에서 일했는데요 지금은 한국어를 공부하려고 한국어학당에 다녀요. 한국어를 공부한 지 여섯 달 됐어요. 대학교에서는 신문방송학을 전공했고요.  
Man: Hello. I am Alex from America. I used to work in a broadcasting station in America but now I am attending the Korean Language Institute to study Korean. It has been six months since I've been studying Korean. I majored in journalism and mass communication in college.

여자: 만나서 반가워요. 저는 김미선이에요. 무역회사에서 일하고 있어요. 대학교에서는 경영학을 전공했고요. 제가 무역회사에서 일해서 회사 일로 가끔 미국에 가요. 영어가 많이 필요한데 알렉스 씨께서 도와주시면 좋겠어요.  
Woman: It's nice to meet you. I'm Misun Kim. I work at a trading company. I majored in business administration in college. Since I work at a trading company, I sometimes go to America for work. I really need to practice my English and it would be nice if you could help me.

#### Let's Read

**Personal Statement [Major & Study Plans]**

I majored in Asian Studies at the Berlin University in Germany. After meeting Korean and Chinese friends in senior high school, I became interested in Asian culture so I studied Asian Studies. Then after taking a course on Korean culture in college, I wanted to learn about it in even more detail. That is why I diligently read books on Korean culture and looked for Korean movies and TV programs to watch on my own.

In order to understand Korean culture well, you need to know the Korean language. That is why I came to Korea to study Korean after I graduated from college. It has been about one year since I came to Korea to study Korean. Now I would like to study the Korean culture a little more closely so I am planning on majoring in Korean Studies in graduate school.

There are still many people in Germany who do not know much about Korean culture. If I enter this school, I want to diligently study the Korean culture and understand more about Korea. Then I will introduce this great culture of Korea in Germany.

