## Unit 2

### 제1항 - My Friends
**Lesson objective:** to understand descriptions and introductions about friends

#### Vocabulary
- 잘생기다 - to be good-looking
- 날씬하다 - to be slim
- 똑똑하다 - to be smart
- 목소리가 좋다 - to have a good voice
- 아나운서 - newscaster
- 착하다 - to be good-natured or nice
- 귀엽다 - to be cute
- 어리다 - to be young
- 뚱뚱하다 - to be fat
- 안경을 끼다 - to wear glasses
- 성격이 좋다 - to have a good personality
- 교육학 - educational studies
- 경주 - Gyeongju
- 지루하다 - to be boring or tedious
- 성격이 밝다 - to have a bright personality

#### Let's Listen

**1.**
1) 이거 제 초등학교 때 사진이에요.  
   This is a picture of me when I was in elementary school.

2) 제 친구는 한국 사람인데 미국에서 10년 살았어요.  
   My friend is Korean but lived in America for ten years.

3) 제 동생 사진이에요. 항상 엄마 일을 많이 도와 드려요.  
   This is a picture of my younger sister. She is always helping my mom with her work.

4) 우리 집 강아지예요. 우리 강아지는 많이 먹는데 운동을 안 해요.  
   This is my family's dog. My dog eats so much but doesn't exercise.

**2.**
1) 저는 오전에는 한국어를 배우고 오후에는 아르바이트를 해요.  
   I learn Korean in the morning and in the afternoon I work part-time.

2) 제 친구는 성격이 좋고 재미있어요.  
   My friend has a good personality and is fun.

3) 저는 어제 잠을 못 잤어요.  
   I couldn't sleep last night.

4) 지난 주말에 오랜만에 고등학교 친구를 만났어요.  
   I met a high school friend last weekend after a long while of not seeing him.

**3-4.**
에릭: 리타오 씨, 잘 지냈어요? 옆에 있는 분은 누구예요?  
Eric: How are you, Letao? Who is the person next to you?

리타오: 제 고향 친구예요. 지금 대학원에서 교육학을 공부하고 있어요. 아주 똑똑하고 성격도 좋아요. 키도 크고 예쁘지요?  
Letao: That is my friend from my hometown. She is studying educational studies in graduate school. She is really smart and has a great personality, too. She's also tall and pretty, don't you think?

왕샤오링: 저는 왕샤오링이에요. 리타오한테서 이야기를 많이 들었어요. 회사에서 일도 하고 공부도 해서 많이 바쁘시겠어요.  
Wangshaoling: I'm Wangshaoling. I heard a lot about you from Letao. You must be very busy working in a company and studying.

에릭: 조금 바쁘지만 한국어 공부가 재미있어요. 시간이 있으면 리타오 씨하고 우리 회사 근처로 저녁 먹으러 오세요.  
Eric: I am a bit busy but studying Korean is fun. Please come over with Letao to have dinner near my workplace when you have time.

**5-7.**
유키: 흐엉 씨, 이 사진은 지난달에 친구들과 경주에 여행 가서 찍은 사진이에요.  
Yuki: Huang, this is a picture I took with my friends when we traveled to Gyeongju last month.

흐엉: 유키 씨 옆에 있는 사람이 누구예요? 눈이 크고 귀엽네요.  
Huang: Who is this person next to you, Yuki? Her eyes are big and cute.

유키: 어학당 친구가 소개해 준 한국 친구 미선 씨예요. 연세대학교 학생인데 친절하고 성격이 아주 밝아요.  
Yuki: That is my Korean friend Misun who was introduced to me by my friend from the Language Institute. She is a student of Yonsei University. She's very nice and has a bright personality.

흐엉: 그런데 여기 키가 크고 머리가 짧은 남자는 누구예요?  
Huang: Who is this tall man with the short hair?

유키: 이번에 처음 만났는데 미선 씨의 대학교 친구 영수 씨예요. 경주 사람이어서 우리에게 경주를 소개해줬어요. 아주 재미있는 친구예요.  
Yuki: I met him for the first time during this trip. His name is Youngsu and he is Misun's college friend. Since he is a person from Gyeongju, he introduced the city to us. He is a really fun person.

흐엉: 한국 친구가 많아서 좋겠어요. 저도 한국 친구가 있으면 좋겠어요.  
Huang: It must be nice to have so many Korean friends. I wish I had Korean friends, too.

유키: 흐엉 씨, 다음에 제 친구들과 같이 만나는 게 어때요? 같이 한국 음식도 먹고 한국어로 이야기도 해요.  
Yuki: Huang, what do you think about meeting with my friends next time? We can eat Korean food together and speak in Korean.

#### Let's Read

**I am looking for a friend..**

I am Maria from Russia. I came to Korea three months ago. I learn Korean at the Korean Language Institute in the morning but I don't have much to do in the afternoon after class. There are days I study in the library and some days I take walks at the park.

I spend a lot of time by myself and study by myself because I don't have any friends so there are times when I feel bored. That is why I am looking for a friend I can meet and study with after class and have fun together.

I have a bright personality and I like to talk. I studied in Japan last year and this year, I came to study abroad in Korea. I love Korean music so I listen to it every day and occasionally go to the Noraebang. I hope your hobbies will be like mine and we can go to the Noraebang together.

Please contact me if you want to study together and be friends.

**Comments:**
- So you studied in Japan. You must good in Japanese, too.
- So you like Korean music. I like going to the Noraebang, too, so I'll give you a call.
- I feel bored these days because I don't have any friends, too. I think it will be fun to study and play together.

