### 제2항 - Meeting with family and relatives
**Lesson objective:** to understand introductions of family and relatives and family gatherings

#### Vocabulary
- 조카 - nephew or niece
- 외숙모 - aunt (wife of one's mother's brother)
- 이모부 - uncle (husband of one's mother's sister)
- 큰어머니 - aunt (wife of one's father's older brother)
- 삼촌 - uncle (brother of one's father)
- 외할머니 - grandmother on the mother's side
- 외삼촌 - uncle (brother of one's mother)
- 이모 - aunt (sister of one's mother)
- 외할아버지 - grandfather on the mother's side
- 생신 - birthday in honorific form
- 큰아버지 - uncle (older brother of one's father)
- 친척 - relative
- 돌잔치 - baby's first year birthday party
- 장난감 - toy
- 태어나다 - to be born
- 대전 - Daejeon
- 고모부 - uncle (husband of one's father's sister)
- 작은어머니 - aunt (wife of one's father's younger brother)

#### Let's Listen

**1.**
1) 우리 삼촌은 은행원입니다.  
   My uncle is a bank clerk.

2) 우리 외할머니는 부산 사람입니다.  
   My grandmother is from Busan.

3) 내일 오전에는 맑고 오후에는 조금 흐리겠습니다.  
   There will be clear skies tomorrow morning and then cloudy in the afternoon.

4) 오늘 우리 식당에서 점심은 비빔밥, 저녁은 불고기를 준비하겠습니다.  
   At our restaurant today, we will be preparing bibimbap for lunch and bulgogi for dinner.

**2.**
1) 우리 이모부는 운동을 할 때 음악을 들어요.  
   My uncle listens to music while he exercises.

2) 우리 외삼촌은 밥을 먹을 때 텔레비전을 봐요.  
   My uncle watches television while he eats.

3) 우리 이모는 커피를 마실 때 우유를 넣어요.  
   My aunt adds milk when she drinks coffee.

4) 우리 외할아버지는 신문을 읽을 때 안경을 쓰세요.  
   My grandfather wears glasses when he reads the newspaper.

**3-4.**
존: 윤아 씨, 예쁜 꽃다발이네요. 어디에 가세요?  
John: Yuna, that's a beautiful bouquet of flowers. Where are you going?

윤아: 오늘 할머니 생신이어서 가는 길이에요. 할머니께서 꽃을 아주 좋아하셔서 생신 때마다 장미꽃을 사요.  
Yuna: It's my grandmother's birthday today so I'm on my way to see her. My grandmother loves flowers very much so I always buy her roses on her birthday.

존: 할머니께서 좋아하시겠어요. 그런데 혼자 가세요?  
John: Your grandmother must really like that. But are you going by yourself?

윤아: 부모님은 나중에 오시고, 큰아버지와 큰어머니는 할머니 댁에 오셨을 거예요.  
Yuna: My parents will come later and my uncle and aunt have most likely already arrived.

**5-7.**
에릭: 우진 씨, 주말에 뭐 하셨어요?  
Eric: Woojin, what did you do over the weekend?

우진: 조카의 돌잔치에 다녀왔어요. 오랜만에 가족들과 친척들을 만나서 반가웠어요. 그런데 잘 쉬지 못해서 조금 피곤하네요.  
Woojin: I went to my nephew's first year birthday party. It was so nice to see my family and relatives after such a long time. But I'm a little tired because I didn't get much rest.

에릭: 돌잔치가 뭐예요? 처음 들었어요.  
Eric: What is that first year birthday party? It's my first time hearing about it.

우진: 아이의 첫 번째 생일에 가까운 사람들이 모여서 축하해주는 파티예요. 돌잔치에 갈 때 선물이나 돈을 준비해요. 아이에게 좋은 이야기를 해 주면서 즐겁게 파티를 해요. 맛있는 음식도 먹고요.  
Woojin: It's a party for a baby's first birthday where people who are close to the family come to celebrate. When you attend one of these parties, you prepare a gift or money. The guests enjoy the party as they say nice things to the child. They also eat delicious food.

에릭: 아, 그렇군요. 우진 씨는 무슨 선물을 샀어요?  
Eric: I see. What kind of gift did you buy, Woojin?

우진: 저는 조카가 운동선수가 되면 좋을 것 같아서 장난감 야구공을 샀어요.  
Woojin: I thought it would be great if my nephew grew up to become an athlete so I bought him a baseball toy.

#### Let's Read

I was born in Korea but because I lived in Brazil since I was two years old, I cannot speak Korean very well. My father usually spoke to me in Korean so my listening was alright but speaking was difficult.

It's been three months since I came to Korea and now I feel a little more used to speaking in Korean.

Last weekend, there was my aunt's wedding from my father's side. My uncle's hometown is in Daejeon so the wedding was held there. My grandfather, grandmother, and many relatives came to the wedding and I spoke to them in Korean.

When there was something I didn't know, my aunt, the wife of my father's younger brother, helped me on the side. Although it was a bit difficult, it felt good to be able to speak to my relatives in Korean.

