## Korean Culture: Titles

In Korea, we use titles normally used for family members and relatives to also call other people who are not related to us. For example, for males, many people call an older person who is close to them "형" (older brother to a male) or "누나" (older sister to a male). Sometimes, people call their friend's mother "어머니" (mother) as well.

You can also oftentimes hear people call the server at restaurants "이모" (aunt). If you call people who are not your family members as if they were, it helps you become closer in relationship.

