**Japchae (Clear Noodles Stir-fried with Beef and Vegetables)**

Have you ever tried cooking japchae? This is a dish that is always eaten at parties in Korea. Shall we try making japchae?

**Ingredients:** clear noodles, beef, mushroom, carrot, onion, spinach, egg

**Seasoning:** minced garlic, sesame oil, soy sauce, salt, sugar, black pepper

Put in the garlic, soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, and black pepper with the meat and mix.

Place the spinach into boiling water and remove them after one minute. Then season the spinach with minced garlic and salt.

Fry the eggs in a thin layer and then cut them. Cut up the onions, mushrooms, and carrots.

First, fry the onions. Then separately fry the carrots, mushrooms, and meat.

Boil the clear noodles for about 6-7 minutes. Pan-fry the noodles with some soy sauce.

Mix in the pan-fried vegetables and meat with the noodles. Sprinkle soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar, or black pepper if needed.

