## Korean Culture: Gwangjang Market

The Gwangjang Market is an old marketplace over 100 years old in the Jongno region of Seoul. There are many tourists from foreign countries because it is in the middle of Seoul and this market has been loved by Koreans for a long time.

There are quite a lot of traditional Korean dress stores and blanket stores. It is especially famous for the eatery alleys where you can eat a variety of Korean cuisine. Because Korean traditional food like bindaetteok (mung-bean pancake), bibimbap, gimbap, and yukhoe (steak tartare) are so famous, the alleys are so busy with the footsteps of the people looking for these types of food all day.

