## Korean Culture: Housewarming Gifts

Korean people usually give tissue paper, soap, detergent, and other similar living products as housewarming gifts. The tissue paper is a gift with the meaning of wishing that all bad incidents be wiped away and that all things turn out for the good. The soap or detergent means you wish that a lot of money will be made and many good things will arise just as soap bubbles rise.

However, there are gifts that you should not give at a housewarming. You do not give knives or scissors as gifts because they carry the meaning of cutting off a relationship with someone.

